  "interpretation_limits": [
    "This audit uses real archived normal/random top5 for the same 500 dev clips and identical trained checkpoint; bank-pair samples describe only bank geometry.",
    "Actual dev query feature vectors were not archived, so query-to-key cosine, query-neighbor margins, query directions, and query-conditioned attention cannot be measured here. Fit records are not substituted as pseudo-dev queries.",
    "Value-mean similarity does not establish Adapter attention output, token similarity, gradient sensitivity, or causal irrelevance; those require the separate real-dev AV+Adapter diagnostic.",
    "Raw bank cosine can be high because of a shared global direction; centered diagnostic cosines remove only the bank mean and are not the production retrieval score.",
    "Rank-aligned pair distances are omitted: Adapter key/value attention is permutation invariant over the neighbor set. Cross-set nearest cosines and unordered intersections are descriptive, not an assignment of causal correspondence.",
    "group_id currently equals clip ID, so no-self/no-same-group does not certify no cross-clip source duplicates.",
    "No new generation or official rescoring was performed; output comparisons and per-sample F1 come from existing intervention reports."
  ],
  "conditional_next_steps": [
    "Inspect real-dev adapter outputs before changing geometry or training: if selected-value differences shrink strongly through V_MLP/attention/output projection, locate that stage with the separate diagnostic.",
    "If raw value means are close but centered means differ, do not equate high raw cosine with identical information; compare actual projected tokens under the same query.",
    "Do not change learning rate or expand training solely from this CPU bank geometry; decide a single targeted intervention after AV+Adapter evidence."
  ],
